# The all-in: fight in the first minutes or not at all.
#
# Built for the Impossible question (3.7x income): every measured match at
# that rung ended defeated or wiped -- 0/12, and the bot never reached the
# enemy base ([[policy-holding-ground]]). Against an opponent whose advantage
# compounds with time, the earliest possible fight is the fairest one, so
# this doctrine spends nothing on a future it will not have: one extractor,
# tanks immediately, three-tank waves, and the rush verb marching every
# released wave at the mirror of our base until contact.
#
# Deliberately NOT one field from the champion. This is a composition
# question -- "can any doctrine beat Impossible" -- and the champion rides in
# the same batch as its control.

name rush
goals extractorT1,c_tank,c_tank,c_tank
max_workers 2
mass 3
reserve 0
expand 1
counter 0
cover 0
intercept 0
guard_cap 0
aa_cover 0
forward 0
scout 0
raid 0
rush 1
creep 0
riposte 0
tech 0
